json5p/pointer
description: A * dereference - the value is another node, named by a quoted colon path
- >
  A **pointer** is `*` followed by a quoted **colon path** - the value IS the node the path
  names, a shared edge rather than a copy. More colons at the start widen the scope - bare is
  the current mapping (a sibling), `:` the document root, `::` the project, `:::` the world. A
  bare integer portion selects a position, a worded or quoted portion a key, and a backslash
  (doubled inside the double-quoted string) makes a character literal - `\:` a colon, `\.\.` the
  literal key `..`:
- !!<format: text/x-json5p> |
  feline: *"pets: 1",            // a sibling's position 1
  topDog: *": pets: 0",          // from the document root
  secondName: *"pets: 1: name",  // ...then the key "name" inside it
- >
  The root of a document is always a node - a top-level pointer is not allowed.
